cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SPIN-73 reconstructed: aerodynamic coefficients of spin-stabilized projectiles"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it, and cite the original SPIN-73
  report it reconstructs (see references).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "de Padua Sanches"
    given-names: "Luiz Guilherme"
repository-code: "https://github.com/OAfundador/aeroballistics"
license: MIT
version: "0.5.0"
abstract: >-
  A Python reconstruction of SPIN-73 (Whyte, Picatinny Arsenal TR 4588,
  1973), which estimates the aerodynamic coefficients of a spin-stabilized
  projectile from its geometry alone and runs a stability analysis. The
  equations, the empirical DATA blocks and the program logic were read from
  the scanned report and checked against the 13 output tables it printed in
  1973. Optional, separate additions: modern-convention output, metric
  inputs, mass-property estimation, and an empirical free-flight correction.
  Usable as a library by 6DOF trajectory simulators.
keywords:
  - exterior ballistics
  - aerodynamic coefficients
  - spin-stabilized projectiles
  - SPIN-73
  - 6-DOF
references:
  - type: report
    title: "SPIN-73, an Updated Version of the SPINNER Computer Program"
    authors:
      - family-names: Whyte
        given-names: R. H.
    institution:
      name: Picatinny Arsenal
    number: "Technical Report 4588"
    year: 1973
    notes: "DTIC AD0915628. Distribution A: approved for public release."
